# Structured question popups (dual-host)

Call the **host structured question tool** — whichever exists in the
current tool schema:

| Host | Tool | UX |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Cursor** | **AskQuestion** | Clickable choices in chat |
| **Claude Code** | **AskQuestion** (Cursor) / **AskUserQuestion** (Claude Code) | Claude's native picker |

Detect by tool availability, not by guessing the product name. Prefer
the tool that is present. Never invent a third question API.

Upstream VGV skills may say **AskQuestion** (Cursor) / **AskUserQuestion** (Claude Code) (Claude-first) or the
dual-host dialect. On Cursor, treat AskQuestion (Cursor; AskUserQuestion on Claude Code) mentions as
**AskQuestion**.

## Required behavior

When a skill, rule, or workflow says to present options, confirm a
choice, or ask a clarifying multiple-choice question:

1. Call **AskQuestion** if it is in the tool schema; otherwise call
   **AskQuestion** (Cursor) / **AskUserQuestion** (Claude Code) if that is available.
2. Mark the recommended option clearly (e.g. "(Recommended)").
3. Do **not** paste the option list as plain chat text when either
   structured question tool is available. Numbered "1. 2. 3." chat
   lists are the last-resort fallback only — never the intended UX.
4. On Cursor, present the skill's option list but **drop Claude twins
   the port collapsed**: never show both `Plan now` and
   `Continue with planning`, or both `Build now` and `Start building`.
   Canonical Cursor lists live in `vgv-cursor-handoff.mdc`.
5. Translate Claude-only context-reset actions on Cursor into same-chat
   actions: `Plan now` → `Plan now`;
   `Build now` → `Build now`. On Claude Code, clear-context
   handoffs remain valid when the skill requests them.
6. After a Cursor handoff selection, invoke the next skill immediately
   in the current chat. Never emit `/clear`, `/new-chat`, or copy-paste
   commands on Cursor.
7. If **neither** structured question tool is available (e.g. **Grok
   4.5** on Cursor), say so once, tell the user which model restores
   the clickable picker (**Composer 2.5 recommended** for brainstorm/plan
   handoffs; Claude or GPT also work), then list the same options as a
   numbered chat list (last resort only).

For brainstorm / plan / refine sessions on Cursor, prefer **Composer
2.5** as the parent model so AskQuestion is available without burning
the Other Models pool. Subagent model pins are separate — see
`vgv-cursor-handoff.mdc`.

## Handoff options

Post-brainstorm / post-plan / post-build option lists come from the
active skill's SKILL.md. Present them via the host structured question
tool, then execute the pick per `vgv-cursor-handoff.mdc` (Cursor) or
the skill's clear-context handoff (Claude Code).
